  "reason": "1) Evidence/uncertainty: Only one experiment is complete (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → acc 0.485, F1 0.464). We have no information about whether the image modality carries useful signal, making it impossible to judge whether multimodal fusion is worth the added complexity. 2) What this tests: config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is a clean unimodal ablation that directly measures the standalone predictive power of the image branch. Because it mirrors config_001's singleprofile setting and uses the 'default' encoder for its modality (resnet50 ↔ pca_n2000), the comparison isolates the modality effect. 3) Why best next experiment: Under a tight budget, the single most consequential design question is whether the image modality adds information beyond RNA. If image_only substantially outperforms or underperforms rna_only, it immediately reshapes the search (e.g., prioritize multimodal with the stronger modality, or deprioritize image encoders entirely). This one experiment reduces the largest source of uncertainty and will make every subsequent multimodal or encoder-choice experiment far more interpretable, making it the highest-information-value use of the next slot."
